blocks.body:
A \emph{regular four-edge anchor} for a word $\kappa$ consists of a frame
  (\cref{def:four_active_frame}) and half-lengths $L\in\RR^4$ with
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item $L_j>0$ for every $j$;
    \item the strict endpoint bounds $s_jL_j<1$ and $t_jL_j<1$ for every
      $j$ (eight inequalities on literal readings);
    \item $C(L)=0$;
    \item $DC(L)\colon\RR^4\to\CC\times\RR$ is surjective.
  \end{enumerate}
  The structure does not require any reading of $\kappa$ to be positive;
  positivity of the \emph{whole} word is a hypothesis of the realization
  theorem \cref{thm:regular_four_anchor_realizes}.

lean.code:
theorem realizesR2 {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] {κ : ZMod n → ℝ}
    (A : RegularFourAnchor κ) (hκ : ∀ i, 0 < κ i) : RealizesR2 κ :=
  A.frame.realizesR2_of_controller_regular hκ A.positive A.start_lt A.finish_lt A.zero A.regular
